# PharmaApp

**PharmaApp** is an offline **Medical Store Management System** built with the **MERN stack** (MongoDB, Express, React, Node.js) and packaged as a **desktop application using Electron**. It allows store owners to manage inventory, sales, purchases, suppliers, and generate invoices without an internet connection.

---

## Features

- **Inventory Management:** Add, update, and track medicines and products.
- **Sales & Purchase Management:** Record daily sales and purchases.
- **Supplier Management:** Add and manage suppliers.
- **Invoice Generation:** Generate printable invoices for sales.
- **Backup & Restore:** Create backups of your database.
- **Offline Support:** Fully functional without internet.
- **Electron Desktop App:** Cross-platform desktop application for Windows.

---

## Tech Stack

- **Frontend:** React.js
- **Backend:** Node.js + Express.js
- **Database:** MongoDB (local)
- **Authentication:** JWT
- **Desktop Packaging:** Electron, Electron Builder
- **Styling:** CSS, HTML

---

## Installation

1. **Clone the repository**

```bash
git clone https://github.com/mustu633/Pharma.git
cd PharmaApp
Install dependencies
npm install

Start the app in development
npm start

This will open the Electron app with backend server running locally.

Build for production

bash
Copy code
npm run build
This will package the app into a Windows executable using Electron Builder.

Environment Variables
Create a .env file 


